# OnePlus 15 (kaanapali): the panel is the only console. No serial port is
# wired out on this board and there is no USB gadget yet, so route all
# output to the video console. stdin is assigned the always-registered
# "serial" stdio stub, which never produces input; it exists so console
# setup has an input device to attach.
stdin=serial
stdout=vidconsole
stderr=vidconsole

# M3 autorun: boot NixOS from the ex01_esp FAT partition via
# sysboot/extlinux. The boot source is pinned by PARTLABEL to ex01_esp
# (a partition we created); there is no scan-anything fallback in this
# image. Verbs used are exactly {bootdev, part, printenv, echo, sysboot}.
#
# Load addresses (kernel_addr_r, ramdisk_addr_r, fdt_addr_r, scriptaddr)
# are deliberately NOT set here: mach-snapdragon's board_late_init()
# allocates them at runtime out of ABL's real memory map via LMB (which
# honours /reserved-memory, including the splash carve-out) and its
# env_set_hex() calls would override any value written here anyway --
# initr_env runs before board_late_init. The printenv makes the chosen
# addresses visible on the panel before the long PWM-speed load.
#
# If sysboot returns, every label failed (fail-closed FDT policy included);
# the final echo makes that landing explicit instead of a bare dead prompt.
bootcmd=bootdev hunt scsi; \
part number scsi 0 ex01_esp esp_num; \
printenv esp_num scriptaddr kernel_addr_r ramdisk_addr_r fdt_addr_r; \
echo M3: loading NixOS from ex01_esp over PWM-speed UFS - minutes of silence are EXPECTED; \
sysboot scsi 0:${esp_num} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
echo M3 bootcmd fell through - sysboot did not boot any label
